  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\nIssued at 1219 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nWelcome to the long, holiday weekend featuring well above-normal\ntemperatures and persistently dry conditions for much of the Mid-\nSouth. Temperatures have already risen into the mid to upper 90s\nby midday, with a few locations exceeding 100 degrees already.\nHeat Index values have already climbed over 105 for many as well.\nHigh temperatures are expected to top out in the upper 90s to low\n100s across the area both today and tomorrow, which for those\nkeeping track is around 10 degrees above normal. With the\ndangerous heat continuing, a Heat Advisory remains in effect for\nall of the Mid-South through 8 PM Sunday. With this in mind, an\nargument could be made that a few locations may not reach\n105 degrees tomorrow, mainly along the TN River. The uncertainty\nalong the TN River generally exists due to a back door frontal\nboundary that will be moving through the area. However, the\ntiming of this is still somewhat uncertain and how quickly the\n\"cooler\" air will be able to filter in behind. As such, opted to\nleave the areawide Heat Advisory in place for now. Outside of\nthis, there is a low chance (generally < 20%) of diurnally-driven\nafternoon thunderstorms both this afternoon and again Sunday\nafternoon mainly across north MS. Unfortunately, this will likely\nprovide little relief to the ongoing, oppressive heat.\n\nInto Monday, a back door frontal boundary will have cleared the\narea, allowing temperatures to fall back a few degrees. While\nthis will lead to conditions drying out further, an upper-level\nridge across the region will keep temperatures well above-normal\nfor early to mid September. As such, no measurable precipitation\nis in the forecast through at least the middle of the week, with\nhigh temperatures remaining in the mid to upper 90s. With the dry\nconditions, heat index values will likely top out just below\n105 for most of the area outside of the Delta region. While heat\nindex values may approach to exceed 105 degrees for the Delta,\nconfidence remains generally low and any heat headlines will be\nhandled on a day to day basis if needed.\n\nBy the middle to end of next week, this upper-level ridge will\nfinally begin to break down, potentially allowing for a small\npattern shift. LREF guidance currently shows spread amongst \nmembers growing particularly by the end of next week, so general\nforecast confidence is low. However, even with the spread amongst\nmembers, guidance does keep the Mid-South in a generally above-\nnormal temperature pattern as we head into next weekend. So,\nwhile PoP chances may return by the end of next week, the heat is\ncertainly here to stay unfortunately.",
